    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "We can remove this, but the `tools` coming from the `useChat` hook cannot be used for the `ChatUiComponent` because the type is incorrect. This is because we are missing `layoutComponent` and `addToolResults` (we add these in the widget for IS.js).\r\n\r\n- The `layout` template is optional for IS.js, but `layoutComponent` is required for RIS. Do we want to address this, or is it expected?\r\n- Should we move the `tools` with `addToolResult` in the `connectChat` connector?\r\n\r\ncc @Haroenv ",
    "commit_id": "148e77147c818c61f507278eb88d6348099a8e76",
    "created_at": "2025-11-06T16:54:51Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -187,14 +184,23 @@ export function Chat<\n     isClearing,\n     clearMessages,\n     onClearTransitionEnd,\n-    tools: hookTools,\n+    addToolResult,\n   } = useChat({\n     ...props,\n-    defaultOpen,\n     tools,\n-    sendAutomaticallyWhen: lastAssistantMessageIsCompleteWithToolCalls,\n   });\n \n+  const toolsForUi = React.useMemo(() => {\n+    const result: Record<string, any> = {};\n+    Object.keys(tools).forEach((key) => {\n+      result[key] = {\n+        ...tools[key],\n+        addToolResult,\n+      };\n+    });\n+    return result;\n+  }, [tools, addToolResult]);",
